35006
ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 35006, Nov. 19, 2024>
Article 1 ( Enforcement date )
This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 ( Applicability to retention and destruction of drivers' licenses )
The amended provisions of Article 52-2 shall also apply to drivers' licenses retained as at the time this Decree enters into force; provided, notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 52-2(2)4, the commissioner of a City/Do police agency, the chief of a police station, and the Korea Road Traffic Authority shall destroy the relevant drivers' licenses retained as at the time this Decree enters into force if they are not retrieved until three years after the enforcement of this Decree, notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 52-2(2)4.
Article 3 ( Applicability to partial exemption from driver's license tests )
(1) The amended provisions of subparagraphs 18 and 19 of Appendix 3 shall begin to apply to those who pass skill examinations after this Decree enters into force.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of subparagraphs 18 and 19 of Appendix 3, a person who has passed a skill examination before this Decree enters into force shall be exempted from a skill test on test course or on-road driving test pursuant to subparagraph 18 or 19 of the previous Appendix 3 for one year from the date this Decree enters into force.
Article 4 ( Special cases concerning postponement of issuance of renewed drivers' licenses and regular aptitude tests )
A person whose driver's license renewal period has been postponed pursuant to the previous Article 55 as at the time this Decree enters into force (excluding those who have been issued renewed driver's licenses) shall have his or her driver's license renewed and issued within three years from the date this Decree enters into force.
Article 5 ( Special cases concerning postponement of occasional aptitude tests )
A person (excluding those who have undergone an occasional aptitude test) whose occasional aptitude test has been postponed pursuant to the previous Article 57 as at the time this Decree enters into force shall undergo an occasional aptitude test within one year from the date this Decree enters into force.

